agy fixtures: documented, not recorded.

The fixtures are synthesised from the documentation of 2026-11-15.

No live agy ran for the antigravity programme's unattended goal. Every agy
text in the tests is synthesised from Google's Antigravity CLI documentation
and the numbers it prints, so what the tests prove is mc's reading of the
documented shapes, not agy's behaviour. A recorded output, when one exists,
replaces the synthesis here and the parse below is judged against it.

Output (tests/mc/run-plan.test.js, the agy-stream reader; stream-success.ndjson and json-success.json here)
  stream-json   NDJSON events `init`, `step_update` and `result`, each payload
                under its own name: `result.status`, `.response`,
                `.num_turns`, `.usage`, `.error`; the conversation id on the
                event or in `init`.
  json          the one terminal object, unwrapped, with the same fields.
  Tokens        the documented example: input 10415, output 657 (thinking 616
                is inside it), cache reads 8113; the two-turn example's second
                step: input 278 beside cache reads 30214. `input_tokens` is the
                uncached input and is never reduced by cache reads.
  Failure       a status other than SUCCESS, an `error`, a non-zero exit and an
                empty stdout at exit 0 are each a failed session. A sign-in or
                locked-keyring message is a login interruption.

Plan quota (tests/mc/agy-capacity.test.js, `agy -p /usage --output-format text`)
  ASSUMED format (R3): per model group a heading line, then
      Five Hour Limit Remaining: 72% (resets 2026-11-15T16:00:00Z)
      Weekly Limit Remaining: 40% (resets 2026-11-20T00:00:00Z)
  The reset may also read "resets in 2h 30m", or sit on the line below; it may
  be absent. The parse takes only a percentage 0-100 beside those two names. A
  window with no printed reset is not stored; one at its limit with none is a
  refusal for QUOTA_SLEEP_MS. Output with no such line is a failed read.

Recorded (tests/mc/run-plan.test.js, the agy-stream reader)
  network-20261117T191632Z.json.err, network-20261117T192619Z.json.err: the
  stderr of two agy reviews of org-detail/hero-scene-card on 2026-11-17
  (runner log goal-org-detail-hero-scene-card-…), copied unchanged. Each
  ended at exit 3 on "There was a network issue connecting to the server" and
  `dial tcp: lookup … server misbehaving`; they read as `offline`.

Recorded hook input (tests/mc/hooks.test.js, tests/adapters/antigravity-cli.test.js,
tests/mc/commands/hook-install.test.js)
  pretool-write_file-goal-20261124T2029Z.json,
  pretool-write_file-notes-20261124T2029Z.json: the PreToolUse stdin of two
  `write_file` calls, saved by a hook whose command wrote its stdin to a file,
  from one agy 1.5.16 session (gemini-3.8-flash-medium) in a scratch directory
  on 2026-11-24, copied unchanged. The first writes
  `<cwd>/programs/demo/goals/one/GOAL.json`, the second `<cwd>/notes.txt`; the
  path is `toolCall.args.Path`. agy's transcripts on this host hold `write_file`
  (args Content, Path, sometimes Overwrite) and `edit_file` (Path, Target,
  Replacement), and no `write_to_file`.
